  "note": "Engine-owned L2 occupancy. Durations scale with gross area only. D = max(b_min, ceil(b0 × (area/plate_ref_m2)^area_exponent)). b_max, when present, is scaled on the SAME exponent (b_max_ref_days at the reference plate). Q/R/C is diagnostic only. Do not ask the client to lock b0. b0 is the TRADE'S OWN DURATION at plate_ref_m2 (3000 m2). RULED/CLARIFIED by PM 2026-09-23: the PM's phrase 「板块节拍」 means exactly these per-trade durations — PM wording 「B0当然是板块节拍啊」 then 「我意思就是说 他们这些工序的工期啦」. There is NO separate 'beat vs whole-floor completion time' dichotomy; that framing was ours, it created a phantom open question, and it is now CLOSED. b_min / b0 / b_max = the PM-填 form's 下限 / b0 / 上限 columns, one-to-one. Recorded in derivation_policy.pm_rulings_2026_09_23. CORRECTION 2026-09-23: an earlier revision of this field claimed the whole-floor demolition figure (~28d at 3000㎡) was an independent check that b0 cannot be a completion time. That reasoning is WITHDRAWN — the figure is an artefact of trade_capacity's deliberately conservative workfront assumption (1 crew per 2000㎡ workfront; multi-crew parallelism withheld pending contractor evidence). The same package's productivity_rates.crew_scaling gives 4d for the identical case: an 8x spread is a config conflict, not a validation. The b0 question is settled by the PM's ruling, NOT by that withdrawn number, which is kept here only for traceability. 13 packages signed by PM 2026-09-23; contract-basis upgrade APPROVED by PM 2026-09-23. feature_ceiling / glass_partition quantities ruled PARTIAL by PM same day (trade_capacity.quantity_scope_ruling_2026_09_23).",
